Usage:
  bqto                                     pick a profile, or start the wizard

  bqto connect [flags] [-- CMD ARGS...]    open a session; see bqto connect -h
  bqto connect PROFILE[,PROFILE...]        open saved profiles
  bqto connect --stack NAME                open every profile of a stack

  bqto profile create|list|show|rename|rm  save and manage profiles
  bqto stack create|list|show|rename|rm    save and manage stacks

  bqto completion bash|zsh|fish            print a shell completion script
  bqto version [--output json]             show the version and any new release
  bqto update                              replace bqto with the newest release

Examples:
  bqto connect --project P --service cloudsql --instance orders
      open a tunnel; the ready: line shows the local port

  bqto connect --project P --service cloudsql --instance orders -- psql -U app
      run psql through the tunnel, then end the session

  bqto connect --project P --service cloudsql --instance orders --save db
      connect, and save the session as the profile db

  bqto profile create cache --project P --service redis --instance cache
      save a profile without connecting

  bqto connect db
      open a profile by name

  bqto stack create work --profile db --profile cache
      group profiles into a stack

  bqto connect --stack work
      open every profile of the stack through one bastion

Put --debug before any command, or set BQTO_DEBUG=1, to print each Google API
call, gcloud command and retry to stderr. Run 'bqto connect --help' for connect
flags.
